Z||000000||glava2876||05-02-2001||10:24 PM||||I ran the tests everyone told me about -plus picked up a manual. My fuel problem boiled down to the fact that the fuel pump wasn't pushing fuel. I pulled the tank and the problems that result from sitting for 10 years with only about 1/4 tank of gas are not fixed by adding new gas, injector cleaner, dry gas etc. The screen was plugged with a fine rust colored silt. The fuellevel was just about even with the plastic baffle. Spraying WD-40 broke up the slime on the baffle. The tank didn't look rusty in the portions that I can see with a flash light, but you can't see it all. Can this tank be saved or is it time to buy a new one -if so, where and how much should it cost? Also, the tank has no visible damage, but the top portion of the plastic baffle was broken off on one side and came out when I dumped the gas. Lastly, I noticed that the outer shell of the cat.converter is rusted away, but the part under it is solid -is it possible to make a cover? Thanks, Glen PS:I can't wait to get this thing running!   ||||reg||5
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||05-02-2001||10:31 PM||||Have the tank cleaned, dipped, hot tanked, boilded out??  Is it the heat sheild that has rust? if so that's no biggie, replace it<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||3
Z||000002||glava2876||05-02-2001||10:57 PM||||Thanks, I'll look in the Yellow pages and call about getting the tank done. The cat is the outer covering, not the shield. The cat. appears to have two layers. Thanks, Glen ||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||05-02-2001||11:08 PM||||If the heat shield is gone off the catalyst replace it. <P>If you mean the skin of the catalyst is gone, replace the cat. Do Not try to repair it.||||reg||1
